WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:05.220
Ingestion is where a RAG system first has the chance to preserve permission context.

2
00:00:05.320 --> 00:00:13.000
A connector may read from a document repository, ticketing system, drive, wiki, database, or case management tool.

3
00:00:13.100 --> 00:00:17.580
The text matters, but the access metadata around the text matters just as much.

4
00:00:17.680 --> 00:00:22.400
Without that metadata, later stages may not know who is allowed to use the content.

5
00:00:22.680 --> 00:00:40.440
Useful metadata can include document origin, repository, owner, tenant, project, classification, access control list, sharing settings, source identifier, source URL, lifecycle state, ingestion time, update time, and deletion status.

6
00:00:40.540 --> 00:00:43.020
Some systems have simple permissions.

7
00:00:43.120 --> 00:00:49.600
Others have inherited permissions, groups, labels, exceptions, or time-bound access.

8
00:00:49.700 --> 00:00:55.700
The ingestion process should capture enough information to support the permission decision that retrieval will need later.

9
00:00:55.980 --> 00:00:59.340
A chunk without permission context is risky.

10
00:00:59.440 --> 00:01:05.440
If only the text moves forward, the index may treat private content like generic reference material.

11
00:01:05.540 --> 00:01:11.220
If stale content keeps a current-looking record, users may receive guidance that should have been retired.

12
00:01:11.320 --> 00:01:17.240
If deleted content remains searchable, the RAG system can outlive the source repository's intended control.

13
00:01:17.520 --> 00:01:24.880
Good ingestion design preserves boundaries between repositories, tenants, projects, and data classifications.

14
00:01:24.980 --> 00:01:30.340
It also records ownership so someone can investigate or correct records later.

15
00:01:30.440 --> 00:01:37.640
Connector behavior should be reviewed like application code because connector shortcuts can create long-lasting permission problems downstream.

16
00:01:37.740 --> 00:01:41.900
Metadata quality is the foundation for reliable authorization.
